  "mechanism": "Strict native IndexedDB exclusion before renderer factory allocation, typed storage-access initiation and DevTools data/observer operations. Browser partition construction omits IndexedDBContextImpl, its task runner and quota client. A small administrative endpoint retains partition lifetime handling and records/disconnects forbidden data operations. Host restoration/snapshot checks run before effects, including runner defaults. Original native attempt journals make caught violations fail teardown.",
  "decision": "Retain private IndexedDB exclusion and browser-service omission with the tested boundaries. TodoMVC can omit IndexedDB. SVGOMG must retain it: its startup bundle acquires the factory even though its code catches exclusion. Keep broader storage/network exclusions unsupported. No application/worker cell meets the predeclared 20% complete-owner reduction in both order blocks. Retain native omission for further architectural work, but do not promote this adapter as a substantial suite speedup. Treat the screen as a local prototype diagnostic, not final performance admission.",
